   with `414 passed in 16.25s` in a disposable lab copy; the live extractor and
   licensed data were not inspected or modified.
+
+## 2026-07-27
+
+- Audited the interrupted Stage A resource pilot without opening candidate or
+  final-holdout data. Gradient-boosting checkpoints were published only after
+  every same-lag trial completed a fold, so an interruption inside the first
+  144-trial group could leave no durable progress. Streamed non-tensor search
+  now invokes the checkpoint callback immediately after each trial-fold result;
+  a simulated disconnect proves a later trial does not start before the earlier
+  trial is persisted.
+- The tensor reference search selected target Ridge at the largest finite alpha
+  for one target. Because Ridge retains an unpenalized intercept, its exact
+  infinite-alpha limit is an intercept-only forecast rather than zero. The
+  prespecified target-Ridge grid now ends with an explicit `intercept_only`
+  natural endpoint, supports target-wise mixtures of finite and intercept-only
+  heads during outer replay, and records the convention in diagnostics. No
+  economic result or protected period informed the change. The complete local
+  code-only suite passed with `420 passed in 21.19s`.
